laurel 3091: LAUREL USB CHECK: RX liveness of the USB gadget while iOS runs. No frame from a configured host for 30 s: 3 ARP asks of the host 2 s apart (its kernel answers for 192.168.7.1), then the RX endpoint ended and armed again (3031's recipe) and one ask, then a gadget restart (RUN/STOP off and on: the host enumerates again, 20 s) and one ask, then a panic with the reason, which lands in fastboot (3090). Any frame ends the check ("RX back after ..."). Rules in bsd/dev/laurel_usb_check_core.h, host test scripts/laurel/usb-check-test.sh. Kill switch laurelusbcheck=0. Both kernels. docs/laurel_sprout/self-recovery.md.

[V 2026-11-07 05:29, 06:37, 06:48] The gadget's RX side died while iOS ran on (3052 has the cause: TRBs on one cache line); the live log kept coming, no panic, no bark, no pong, and the keys were the only way in. The host sends a frame at least every 10 s while scripts/debug/usblog.sh runs (its keepalive), so silence of 30 s from a configured host is the first sign; the ARP reply is the proof the check accepts (rx_frames moves). Costs: a host that sends nothing but answers ARP: one ARP request every 32 s. A host that is gone (not configured) is silence of the normal kind: no check, no panic.

